Z||000008||mbramble||03-08-2000||10:44 AM||||Boy, you guys have me thinking that everything to to with Pontiac &lt;---&gt;Fiero is a conspiracy!!  I just went to the Pontiac.com web site and was looking at the History link.  When I get to the bottom of the 3rd page of timelines, that ends at 1980 -- the "Next" link there takes me back to the first page of timelines.  So, I'm wondering if they ended their history tour at 1980 so they don't have to mention the Fiero!  I try several times and can't get past 1980.  I notice that the 1980 page file name is history_3.html and I keep getting sent back to history.html.  So, I just change it to history_4.html and viola, there it is -- "the Fiero paces the Indy 500, and inspires Pontiac, while defining "Excitement" for the public."  Still, I wonder why the link won't take me to the post 1980 page???  I tried IE and NetScape????||||reg||1
