Z||000026||theogre||03-09-2000||06:51 PM||||Actually this is a comercial site. GM could easily pitch a fit over the logo use.<P>For non comercial use there is "fair use" which is recognized in most of the free world. Basically as long as you acknoledge who owns the copyright you can use it for quite a few non comercial things.<P>There is allot of information about U.S. Copyright law and registration on the <A HREF="http://www.loc.gov/" TARGET=_blank>Library of Congress</A> web site. Most of it is a pretty easy read.<P>For trademark information you have to got to the <A HREF="http://www.uspto.gov/" TARGET=_blank>Patent office.</A> Trademark is a whole diferant set of rules. Trademarking(A.K.A. a DBA name) is also done at a state level, and each state has it's own rules. <P>For example if a car company makes a Altima, and a computer company make an Altima, they don't infring trademark becuase they are 2 completely diferant business. If the both use the same exact logo for the product then they could be in Copyright infrinement, but still not Trademark infringed. (Yes, Nissan and the computer people did fight it out over a name shared by their respective products......)<P>In our case that started this, he's in the car business. That would definatly be a trademark infringement, even if he avoids Copyright infringement.<P>Are you confused enough yet?<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 03-09-2000).]||||reg||1
